---
import Arrow from '../components/Arrow.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import QuoteCta from '../components/QuoteCta.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../data/site';
import { getKeywordTarget } from '../lib/seo-keywords';

const seo = getKeywordTarget('/about/');
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Philadelphia Valet Parking Company"
  description="Learn how Valet Philadelphia, LLC approaches valet parking through site planning, clear handoffs, controlled keys, and accountable shift leadership."
  canonicalPath="/about/"
  image="/images/valet-team-briefing.webp"
  imageAlt="Uniformed valet team reviewing a Philadelphia curb plan before service"
  pageType="AboutPage"
  schema={{
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: siteConfig.url },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'About Valet Philadelphia', item: `${siteConfig.url}/about/` },
    ],
  }}
>
  <section class="site-frame section-gap" aria-labelledby="about-title">
    <div class="panel section-pad bg-paper">
      <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1.12fr_0.88fr] lg:items-end">
        <div>
          <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'About' }]} />
          <p class="eyebrow mt-6">About Valet Philadelphia, LLC</p>
          <h1 id="about-title" class="display-title mt-4 max-w-[13ch]">How a {seo.primaryKeyword} plans each shift.</h1>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="body-large text-ink/70">Guests see a greeting and a returned vehicle. Behind it are {seo.supportingKeywords[0]}, {seo.supportingKeywords[1]}, a defined parking route, assigned staff positions, and a shift lead responsible for live decisions.</p>
          <a href="#approach" class="button-secondary mt-6">Planning approach<Arrow direction="down" /></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="approach" class="site-frame section-gap" aria-labelledby="approach-title">
    <div class="panel section-pad bg-paper">
      <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[0.68fr_1.32fr] lg:gap-14">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Operating method</p>
          <h2 id="approach-title" class="section-title mt-4">Map the site before assigning the crew.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="rich-copy body-large text-ink/68">
          <p>Valet is often described as a convenience. At a busy entrance, it is also a traffic and custody operation. Vehicles arrive at different speeds, guests step into pedestrian space, keys change hands, and parked cars move out of sight.</p>
          <p>Valet Philadelphia begins with those facts. That work happens before service so the guest handoff can remain simple even when the curb, storage route, and timing are not.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-10 grid gap-px overflow-hidden border border-line bg-line md:grid-cols-3">
        <article class="bg-paper p-6 sm:p-8">
          <span class="text-xs font-extrabold text-brick">01</span>
          <h3 class="card-title mt-5">Match the plan to the property.</h3>
          <p class="mt-4 text-ink/64">A narrow city curb, a private drive, and a medical entrance cannot share the same operating assumptions.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="bg-paper p-6 sm:p-8">
          <span class="text-xs font-extrabold text-brick">02</span>
          <h3 class="card-title mt-5">Assign custody.</h3>
          <p class="mt-4 text-ink/64">The ticket, key, vehicle location, guest request, and shift change each need a defined owner.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="bg-paper p-6 sm:p-8">
          <span class="text-xs font-extrabold text-brick">03</span>
          <h3 class="card-title mt-5">Name the shift lead.</h3>
          <p class="mt-4 text-ink/64">Conditions change. The shift lead protects the entrance while adapting the line, route, and retrieval order.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="site-frame section-gap" aria-labelledby="briefing-title">
    <div class="panel grid bg-paper lg:grid-cols-[1.08fr_0.92fr]">
      <div class="relative min-h-[26rem] overflow-hidden lg:min-h-[38rem]">
        <img src="/images/valet-team-briefing.webp" alt="Uniformed valet team reviewing a curb plan during a pre-shift briefing" width="1800" height="1200" loading="lazy" class="absolute inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover" />
      </div>
      <div class="section-pad flex flex-col justify-center">
        <p class="eyebrow">Pre-shift briefing</p>
        <h2 id="briefing-title" class="section-title mt-4">Each attendant starts with an assigned role.</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-ink/66">Before guests arrive, attendants should know the vehicle route, storage zones, key procedure, staff posts, accessibility notes, escalation path, and how the departure rush will be staged.</p>
        <ul class="rule-list mt-6 border-t border-line p-0" role="list">
          {['Curb and pedestrian assignments', 'Key station and ticket checks', 'Radio roles and decision authority', 'Weather, overflow, and closing plan'].map((item) => (
            <li class="flex items-center gap-3 py-4 text-sm font-semibold"><span class="h-2 w-2 bg-signal"></span>{item}</li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="site-frame section-gap" aria-labelledby="standards-title">
    <div class="panel panel-river section-pad">
      <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[0.75fr_1.25fr] lg:gap-14">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Working standards</p>
          <h2 id="standards-title" class="section-title mt-4">Four standards visible during the shift.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="rule-list border-t border-navy/15">
          {[
            ['Identifiable', 'Uniforms and a clear valet position help guests know where to stop and who has accepted the vehicle.'],
            ['Accountable', 'A designated shift lead owns live decisions, communication, and changes to the operating plan.'],
            ['Orderly', 'Keys, tickets, and vehicle locations follow one controlled process throughout the shift.'],
            ['Considerate', 'The setup accounts for pedestrians, accessibility, neighbors, deliveries, rideshare activity, and venue staff.'],
          ].map(([title, body], index) => (
            <article class="grid gap-3 py-6 sm:grid-cols-[3rem_0.7fr_1.3fr] sm:items-start">
              <span class="text-xs font-extrabold text-brick">0{index + 1}</span>
              <h3 class="m-0 text-lg font-bold">{title}</h3>
              <p class="m-0 text-sm text-ink/64">{body}</p>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <QuoteCta eyebrow="Discuss your property" title="Send the entrance, parking route, and schedule." body="Include the expected vehicle volume and the site conditions that affect guest arrival. Those details frame the first operating review." />
</BaseLayout>
